I fixed both errors in `out/w4-C-c3.workflow.json`. The build check now prints `ok` with no ERROR, and the JSON loads.

`{{first_name}}` and `{{last_name}}` are the customer's name, used in the opening line and the identity-confirmation question. Section 2 of the brief lists both as call variables that every call starts with. The workflow just never declared them.

I added a `test_variables` block with `first_name: "Omar"` and `last_name: "Haddad"`, the example values from the brief. This is the workflow's list of default values for call variables, and a real call passes its own values, which take precedence. That was the only edit; I didn't touch any prompt text, node, code hook or rule. I didn't save anything to Freya.

On a test call the agent will ask for "Omar Haddad" unless the call supplies other names.

